2026-11-07T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2483) 'a benchmark measures how many rows one SQLite transaction must carry to keep a FoundationDB-backed store at the challenge's write rate.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2483) 'the 4-process scratch cluster's writer loop, its batch sizes, and the commit-rate table the run produces.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2483) 'How many requests must one SQLite transaction carry so a server on this store keeps up with the challenge's write rate?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2483) 'One SQLite transaction is one FoundationDB transaction, and a commit costs a median of about 8.4 ms, so a server that commits per request caps near 100 writes/s per store. A lone writer through the VFS (the SQLite-on-FoundationDB virtual file system) measured from 89.7 commits/s to 106.9 commits/s, and a bare libfdb_c loop with no SQLite and no VFS measured from 106.5 commits/s to 113.5 commits/s per process at N=1. The challenge's user model is derived, not measured on this server, at about 165 writes/s at 20,000 users and about 830 writes/s at 100,000 users; re-derive from `bench/load.js` before quoting.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2483) 'Run a writer that carries K row-writes in one SQLite transaction, for K = 1, 4, 16, 64, 256, three repeats, in closed-loop and fixed-arrival-rate modes. K=1 must reproduce about 100 commits/s or the probe is wrong. Rows/s must grow close to linearly in K until commit latency rises; that point is the knee.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2483) 'Find the group-commit knee: rows per SQLite transaction against commits and p99
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2483) '- Run the writer on the 4-process scratch cluster (never port 4700), through the VFS, at K = 1, 4, 16, 64, 256, three repeats, in closed-loop and fixed-arrival-rate modes, and record whether any batch's dirty pages crossed into the VFS's staging path (FoundationDB bounds one transaction to 10 MB and 5 s).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2483) '- Build a table from the log files with min, mean and max over the repeats; report rows/s, per-row p99 acknowledge latency, commits over 100 ms, and conflicted delta; name the knee batch size and amend `PROTOCOL.md` with the chosen batch window and size.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2483) '- Run the crash-check control: a planted variant that acknowledges before the commit must show higher throughput and then fail the check; `kill -9` right after an acknowledgement must still find every acknowledged row in the store.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2483  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2483) '- RFD66606-2382, the skateboard's manifest, which names datasource-store's SQLite VFS over FoundationDB as the store this benchmark measures.
